		(property "Description" "GNSS receiver module, UART, LCC 9.7x10.1mm, no on-module SAW/LNA"
			(at 163.83 72.39 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "GNSS module. VIO_SEL left open selects 3.3V. V_BCKP draws 32 uA in hardware backup (Pi off) and ~3 uA running - so a CR2032 on BT1 is roughly 10 MONTHS, not indefinite; losing it costs both hot-start ephemeris and any configuration held in battery-backed RAM. Abs max on that pin is 3.6V. Antenna bias comes from the module's own VCC_RF (VCC - 0.1V = 3.2V) through L1; ICC_RF 100 mA is an ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM and the part has no internal protection, so a shorted coax kills it - the antenna supervisor that would prevent this is deferred to rev 3.0 and needs external MOSFETs plus a sense shunt. Config has three layers: RAM, battery-backed RAM (survives while V_BCKP holds) and a 74-byte one-time-programmable store applied at every startup. Internal LNA has three gain modes - use low gain at 15 dB or more of external antenna gain, bypass at 25 dB or more, to improve immunity against the Pi's WiFi hotspot at 1.575 GHz."
			(at -40.64 13.97 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
